      "hints": [
        "Differentiate: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 - 18x + 24$.",
        "Set $3x^2 - 18x + 24 = -3 \\implies (x-3)^2 = 0 \\implies x = 3$.",
        "Find $y = 6 \\implies A(3,6)$.",
        "Form tangent $y - 6 = -3(x - 3) \\implies y = -3x + 15$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = x^3 - 9x^2 + 24x - 12$ with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 - 18x + 24$$",
        "Equate the derivative to the gradient of the parallel line, $m = -3$:\n$$3x^2 - 18x + 24 = -3 \\implies 3x^2 - 18x + 27 = 0$$\n$$x^2 - 6x + 9 = 0 \\implies (x - 3)^2 = 0 \\implies x = 3$$",
        "Find the $y$-coordinate of the contact point $A$:\n$$y = 3^3 - 9(3^2) + 24(3) - 12 = 27 - 81 + 72 - 12 = 6 \\implies A = (3, \\, 6)$$",
        "Form the equation of the tangent line at $A(3, 6)$:\n$$y - 6 = -3(x - 3) \\implies y = -3x + 9 + 6 \\implies y = -3x + 15$$"
      ],
